[{"body":"The existing `Clarified_rumen_fluid` and `Sludge_fluid` owners carry exact MicrO identities with narrower origin claims than the source contexts establish. Worker05's independent correction review confirmed this while reassessing its assigned source cases; source ownership and all release holds remain unchanged.\n\n| Existing owner | Confirmed scope problem |\n| --- | --- |\n| `data/ingredients/mapped/Clarified_rumen_fluid.yaml`, `MICRO:0000520` | The ontology definition requires cow rumen. Official MediaDive DSMZ161/212 explicitly allow **cow or sheep**, while JCM266/355/1201 describe the preparation without specifying animal species. |\n| `data/ingredients/mapped/Sludge_fluid.yaml`, `MICRO:0000521` | The ontology definition requires municipal sludge. DSMZ119/JCM872 specify anaerobic-digester sludge without that origin; another actual owner context, TOGO M2596, supplies a wastewater origin and a distinct processing sequence. A generic label does not establish municipal origin or make the different preparations equivalent. |\n\nPrimary evidence: [MicrO clarified rumen fluid](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/micro/terms?obo_id=MICRO:0000520), [MicrO sludge fluid](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/micro/terms?obo_id=MICRO:0000521), [DSMZ161 and its clarified-fluid definition](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/161), [DSMZ212](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/medium/212), [JCM266](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=266), [DSMZ119](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium119.pdf), [JCM872](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=872), [TOGO M2596 original context](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2596).\n\nThe isolated worker05 proposals reuse the existing owners under local registry identities, classify them as undefined biological mixtures and preserve distinct supplied preparation descriptions. They do not create duplicate generic owners, equate raw sludge input with the yeast-incubated supernatant, equate raw rumen contents with clarified fluid, or apply one source recipe to every occurrence. No new ambiguous resolving alias is added. Original owner hashes, original ontology evidence, complete occurrence comparisons and first rejected candidate versions remain preserved.\n\nExact evidence and proposed payloads are in `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-05/correction-1193-v1/root/`, with author-separated review in `materials/root-independent-review.json` (SHA256 `4d70637b408acd320aac22441f131b72d8a77911017f1dd515bb2fa787bd7acd`). Findings F03 and its corrected payloads are retained separately. The source case IDs remain bound to the unchanged worker05 shard.\n\nCoordinator follow-up: reconcile overlapping proposals, review the complete integrated owner payload, withdraw unsupported inherited exact MicrO rows if applying the registry correction, and run native synchronization/publication gates. Existing source-specific, owner and export holds remain; the correction review does not grant release approval.\n\nDeduplication: live all-state searches for clarified rumen/sludge found historical #204 (term existence/label verification) and #513 (missing ingredient classification). Neither covers this narrower-origin mismatch. #1193 tracks the worker05 completeness correction; this issue tracks the distinct maintained-owner identity concern. No historical issue is closed or superseded here.\n","number":1204,"state":"open","title":"Reconcile narrower cow and municipal-origin identities on generic fluid owners","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1204"},{"body":"Fresh primary-source review finds an unsupported quantity in the historically approved BSA occurrence. The native companion verifier correctly refuses to publish the fresh WITHHOLD decision while the stored claim still says SUPPORTED.\n\nAffected claim: `MIM.occurrence:8ef56b6e356d256d79632b07d5dd457b18c7d9c99c5d75a540e11c9b34cfc67f`, owned by `data/ingredients/mapped/Bovine_Serum_Albumin.yaml`, source `CultureMech:012955` / MediaDive solution 3888 / JCM220. Current immutable claims source: `reports/ingredient_bundle_20260924/claims.json` (SHA256 `52c5c0e9938725524ed9680c736e1015b74dba1c603c2b76da62b7cc17175a8b`). The complete claim envelope SHA256 is `154a541e80b5e6dcd08c1583795dcb6ae821dc5e6605f42c17d6bf31a2792991`.\n\nThe claim stores `quantity={value: \"9.652509652509652\", unit: \"PERCENT_V_V\"}` and `review_status: SUPPORTED`. Its archived source payload repeats that normalized concentration. [The official JCM220 recipe](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=220) instead specifies 10 mL of 20% bovine serum albumin, fraction V, with 1 L water and separate filtration. [The original MediaDive3888 response](https://mediadive.dsmz.de/rest/solution/3888) captured during the fresh review independently retains amount 10, unit ml, attribute 20%, condition fraction V, `g_l: null`, and reported volume 1036 mL. This supports a source-qualified stock addition; it does not support the current percentage claim or establish a corrected final protein concentration. Do not guess the percentage basis, replacement quantity, product identity or lot.\n\nThe fresh W09 review covers all 20 owners and 51 claims: 49 SUPPORTED, two WITHHOLD. An independent read-only replay verified all 51 native claim proofs, all 20 scoped mapping proofs and the exact source captures, then reproduced the sole mismatch: `Companion claim status disagrees with reviewed disposition`. The existing original review still passes its historical native contract; that deterministic pass is not fresh scientific support for the quantity. The defect is the stored occurrence disposition, not BSA owner identity or a broken native gate.\n\nProposed bounded resolution, after this issue is filed:\n\n- Preserve the historical claims, companion reviews and source captures byte-for-byte. Create a new immutable full 51-claim successor through a guarded, reviewed publication operation; change only this occurrence's `payload.review_status` from SUPPORTED to WITHHOLD. Preserve its stable ID, owner, original quantity, preparation, source payload, evidence references and all other 50 claims. Append a truthful change/provenance receipt outside the historical claims.\n- Review the complete new claim envelope explicitly and bind fresh evidence and its decision to the actual new hash. Do not merely replace a hash in the old approval. The fresh full 20-owner/51-claim companion must bind the final complete canonical review and current owner bytes; the current private 20-row diagnostic base is not a release base.\n- Use existing native `validate_payload`, `validate_review_decision`, `reviewed_products`, the reserved exclusive-output `publish_new_files` primitive, and final `export_bundle`/bundle validation. Recheck all input bytes, role aliases and output reservations. The unchanged-cohort refresher is inapplicable because a scientific claim disposition changes; its guards must remain intact.\n- Preserve the invalid-CAS Lysozyme identifier WITHHOLD, Acriflavine's three chemical-property WITHHOLD findings, and Rifamycin SV's SMILES WITHHOLD finding. Do not drop an owner or claim, transfer historical mapping authority, or turn the source discrepancy into a new chemical identity decision.\n- Test the exact one-field change and preserved 20/51 cohort/IDs; original SUPPORTED payload plus fresh WITHHOLD decision must still fail. Changed owner/proof hashes, omitted or duplicate claims, invalid status, stale inputs and aliased/pre-existing outputs must fail. Verify that the new native bundle retains the withheld observation rather than omitting it.\n\nSource-transform correction in CultureMech, if pursued, is a separate upstream task. This repair neither changes its data nor asserts that a corrected final concentration has been established.\n\nRelated decisions: [#770](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/770) requires preservation of all seven BSA recipe memberships and their preparation context; [#1008](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1008) permits unchanged-cohort refresh only when all selected scientific claims remain identical; [#1057](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1057) preserves the fresh-review boundary; [#753](https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/753) retains the unresolved Lysozyme raw-CAS concern.\n\nLocal exact evidence: `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/fresh-companion-prerequisite-v1/verification-v1.json`, current-claim copy, live issue/comment captures, official-source capture references and immutable W09 review manifest. No claim, source, owner, gate or published review has been changed. The coordinator checked 679 current open and closed issues, the linked issue comments and exact occurrence/finding searches before filing this issue.\n","number":1222,"state":"open","title":"Withhold unsupported JCM220 BSA occurrence quantity through a fresh complete companion","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1222"},{"body":"Found reviewing #863.\n\n`docs/data/label_index.csv` has two `resolved:owned` rows for the label `Fe2(SO4)3 x n H2O`:\n- the preferred term of `kgmicrobe.compound:fe2_so43_x_n_h2o` (MAPPED);\n- a `RAW_TEXT` synonym of `UNMAPPED_0385` (`data/ingredients/unmapped/FeSO43_X_N_H2O.yaml`, preferred term `FeSO43 x n H2O`, 0 occurrences).\n\nclaw's builder keeps the first row, so the label anchors to the mapped record, and #863's rejection-ledger row for CHEBI:53438 applies. If the row order changes, the label would anchor to UNMAPPED_0385, the ledger row would no longer match it, and the anhydrous recipe id could come back through the fallback.\n\nUNMAPPED_0385's own deep-research notes describe the same iron(III) sulfate hydrate. It looks like a duplicate of the mapped record, a merge candidate under the merge-ingredients procedure. At minimum, its `Fe2(SO4)3 x n H2O` synonym should not compete for the mapped record's preferred term.\n","number":873,"state":"open","title":"UNMAPPED_0385 'FeSO43 x n H2O' competes for the Fe2(SO4)3 x n H2O label; the #863 ledger row relies on row order","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/873"},{"body":"Final coordinator review of two published source-review shards found that several no-change outcomes defer already-authorized curation rather than identify a missing scientific fact. Worker04 head `0d2c73e5aee5adb88782537755472d9ca0c5c3cd`; worker08 head `7efd3f8b98f9e822431dcb510c2c242a2569cfc7`; both depend on #1158 at `e000d66`.\n\nConcrete examples:\n\n- Worker08 case `CM_NAME:b9a945a3356d0c885eea986a2f6223e78c8e7d7163ee95629061a640294cbbe8` (H2O deionized) correctly distinguishes deionization from distillation, but its remaining requirement is to perform native owner lookup and use or create the appropriately scoped owner. [DSMZ533](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium533.pdf) explicitly identifies deionized water in both main and trace stock. No proposal or completed lookup disposition accompanies that deferred step.\n- Worker08 case `CM_NAME:e69128522cfe555f63dd51d4a23ece86363290b3839180386b090f368b28d1cc` (glycine-NaOH buffer) preserves a source-defined concentration and pH, and correctly finds a receiving-medium volume transcription error. [JCM906](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=906) specifies the separately prepared buffer. The decision defers representing the stock without explaining which missing fact prevents a bounded preparation identity. It must not be equated to pure glycine or assigned invented titrant amounts.\n- Worker04 case `CM_NAME:2f91fab8feab468a33e48d01e2f0a1363b9ad70816766c69a1e8d68c0ed6f8d5` describes the [NBRC15](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=15) treated, clarified V-8 preparation but defers representing it until later curation. Lack of a molecular mapping or extraction yield does not by itself establish that a source-qualified preparation cannot be represented with an honest partial assertion.\n\nRelated outcomes defer normality-qualified NaOH stocks, source-specific top layers, C9322 supplied-form review, and malted wheat meal because an exact molecular/ontology mapping or later complete-owner review is absent. These are leads for reassessment, not predetermined identity approvals. Genuine solvent, formulation, provenance or supplied-form uncertainties may remain after primary research.\n\nReassess the full no-change cohorts against MAPPING_SEMANTICS sections3/6 and add-media. Complete supported proposal work, or state the precise scientific fact still missing and the actual primary-source searches. Keep receiving-medium dose/unit repair separate from ingredient identity. Never invent concentrations, solvent, chemistry, product equivalence, component completeness, or exact ontology matches; preserve all native holds and old review bytes. Require separate skeptical review of successor evidence/payloads and ordinary commits/pushes on the existing worker branches. No maintained data or export approval is requested from workers.\n\nThis extends the same class of completeness problem seen in #1163 and #1193 to distinct final shards; those earlier findings remain preserved. Exact frozen decisions and capture hashes are retained in the coordinator's immutable `w04-w08-deferred-curation-v1/review-inputs.json` and will accompany the campaign evidence. This is a review-completeness finding, not a statement that every listed source must map.\n","number":1201,"state":"open","title":"Complete deferred source-qualified curation in final unmatched review shards","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1201"},{"body":"Confirmed proposal provenance defect: new agent-authored `ontology_mapping.evidence` entries use `EvidenceTypeEnum.MANUAL_CURATION`, whose maintained schema definition specifically says evidence supplied by a human reviewer. LLM-assisted history does not make that human-source assertion true. No schema or gate change is needed.\n\nWorker08 independent finding **W08-IR-001**, reviewed head `b90a2fd4681d20e2586481b7b9b1114a78281b94`, identifies 95 new/changed entries across 88 selected payloads. Its full review, exact field/value reproductions and authorship receipts are under `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/workers/w03/worktree/.temp/w08-published-head-independent-review-v1/`; findings SHA256 `11e3681d90be88d52a309fc6ed301bcb4c37c749ffb144640175cea6db501af5`. A first unpublished coordinator reconciliation successor independently reproduces the same defect in newly authored mapping evidence. Its original bytes are retained; its attempted separate correction was interrupted before any candidate content was written, and will proceed only after this issue is recorded.\n\nA campaign-wide mechanical scan of the frozen 981-proposal intake flags 698 new entries in 646 proposals across nine worker slots. Those are **audit leads**, not 698 independently confirmed false claims. Worker02 is independently classifying exact before/after entries and actual author/source provenance; current successor changes must be reconciled before final counts. Historical human-supplied evidence must survive.\n\nRequired correction: use the honest source/decision type justified for each new entry (for example LLM_SUGGESTION for agent interpretation, or a direct database/cross-reference type only where its actual evidence warrants it). Preserve exact source URLs, raw values, prior history and all scientific decisions/holds. Apply through guarded writers, retain first attempts, add meaningful regression checks and independently review changed final bytes. Do not transfer inherited owner approval to a changed hash.\n\nDo not perform a global token replacement: `ComponentEvidenceTypeEnum.MANUAL_CURATION` has a different definition; mapping quality, historical manual reviews and genuine human-supplied evidence require separate interpretation. This is a proposal/candidate correction, not a claim that current canonical mappings fail QC.\n\nDeduplication read current all-state searches and full #966/#967/#1217 bodies/comments. #966/#967 concern rendered disclosure and its tests; #1217 concerns a worker06 component/provenance batch. None tracks this cross-campaign new MappingEvidence defect. Relate W08-IR-001 here and keep its other findings separate. No person mentions, release approval or merge.\n","number":1226,"state":"open","title":"Correct human-only mapping evidence types in agent-authored campaign proposals","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1226"},{"body":"Worker-02 continuation of #1201. These are isolated review proposals against the campaign's unchanged maintained owner bytes, not applied data changes. All artifact paths are repository relative. The published predecessor at `58f885fef05f8ff6e8b9b56fcb2479fef23b55c8` remains unchanged.\n\nFour current pure-substance owners accept concentration-qualified or hydration-erasing strings as resolving aliases. The proposed corrections preserve each exact token and original source as `REJECTED_LABEL`; they do not invent stock recipes or change the established solute identities.\n\n| Owner | Tokens made non-resolving | Bounded reason |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `Fe_Nh42_So42_X_6_H2o.yaml` | `Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2 x 6 H2O (0.01% w/v)`, `Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2 x 6 H2O (0.1% w/v)`, `Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2 x 6 H2O (2% v/v)` | Concentration-qualified preparation labels do not unconditionally identify neat Mohr hexahydrate. |\n| `Na-pyruvate.yaml` | `1 M Sodium pyruvate*` | The explicit 1 M preparation is not the neat sodium-pyruvate substance. |\n| `Voso4_X_5_H2o.yaml` | `VOSO4 x 5 H2O (0.01% w/v)`, `VOSO4` | One is preparation-qualified; the other omits the five waters required by the exact hydrate. |\n| `Methanol.yaml` | `Methanol (10%)` | The original stock-strength versus receiving-medium-dose interpretation is unestablished. Either interpretation is unsuitable as an unrestricted molecular-identity alias. |\n\nChEBI 76181, 50144 and 132758 establish the compared solute scopes. They are not evidence for an unstated solvent or a complete formulation. The vanadyl source's CAS12439-96-2 and owner's CAS14708-82-8 differ as annotations; the inspected ChEBI132758 response lists both, so their difference alone is not a chemical contradiction. Preserve both facts rather than silently replacing either.\n\nATCC2883 separately specifies filter-sterilized methanol, 3 mL added after autoclaving. The exact methanol proposal records that source-qualified treatment in notes and supplied_form on the existing molecular owner. It does not create a new mixture from filtration alone or infer assay, dilution, solvent or filter pore size.\n\n\n- Proposal `w02-v2-mohr-hexahydrate-composed`. Current campaign-baseline owner: `data/ingredients/mapped/Fe_Nh42_So42_X_6_H2o.yaml` (SHA256 `ba589668a7e9ed687122766204f51e531d64c54b2177759b555f97be6d7a916f`).\n- Exact proposed payload: `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/continuation-1201-v1/integration/after/Fe_Nh42_So42_X_6_H2o.yaml` (SHA256 `a27f84e2768830f06b85fae4d31f8cc561bcc92467b0070630bafbeefde1b61d`).\n\n- Proposal `c2-proposal-pyruvate-stock-alias`. Current campaign-baseline owner: `data/ingredients/mapped/Na-pyruvate.yaml` (SHA256 `9d0af2a7f4568b68d50c3f766b255892f1e50cd1424236ab96447777ea8da4e4`).\n- Exact proposed payload: `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/continuation-1201-v1/c/proposed-owners/c2-proposal-pyruvate-stock-alias.yaml` (SHA256 `a0dd95f327ce01bdcdd37747eb6e1ed75d311f570ed2e6283ecbbb21690ded11`).\n\n- Proposal `c2-proposal-vanadyl-stock-and-bare-aliases`. Current campaign-baseline owner: `data/ingredients/mapped/Voso4_X_5_H2o.yaml` (SHA256 `2903645ba0ba6c7c0455dc876db9b88bb355d72e0f8a818e269fdfb39800b192`).\n- Exact proposed payload: `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/continuation-1201-v1/c/proposed-owners/c2-proposal-vanadyl-stock-and-bare-aliases.yaml` (SHA256 `3fa275792b65030133f2f375a6e325d08cad3e2a0442f2531ffbd42c5ce5aa08`).\n\n- Proposal `a2-proposal-methanol-source-filtration-provenance`. Current campaign-baseline owner: `data/ingredients/mapped/Methanol.yaml` (SHA256 `a8f09fa01565b9ba9a9caca7a5a78d2ea919bb6c54b26a170a64390caad46a7e`).\n- Exact proposed payload: `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/continuation-1201-v1/a/after-v6/Methanol.yaml` (SHA256 `de3969545ff64b75aa8ded4c783eb37c5db2307348bd09bed3dec7d579f34d08`).\n\n- `CM_NAME:04fc9a1465f3d659efe08a5ae5dad64549020bcf412b8f9ccb55584876555c2c`; source `Fe(SO4)2(NH4)2 . 6H2O`; raw source label `Fe(SO4)2(NH4)2 . 6H2O`.\n- `CM_NAME:12f11ea24b8277a93aa7239dc2e5d98a1ede7a288ecdc58381d46cc339ac5435`; source `Methanol(filter sterilized)`; raw source label `Methanol(filter sterilized)`.\n- `CM_NAME:1bd8d675450108231a5a447707552676245f24c975891b217f1caa5f8170262b`; source `(NH4)2Fe(SO4)2·6H2O`; raw source label `(NH4)2Fe(SO4)2·6H2O`.\n- `CM_NAME:664ea49b4baffce477446f17556f93e233f5535d0abfdec29fbb8f7384caf80c`; source `Fe(SO4)2(NH4)2·6H2O`; raw source label `Fe(SO4)2(NH4)2·6H2O`.\n- `CM_NAME:904d8b9b6ef754a946575436e8d68a149ec7891b40a2e40eb24351912f196097`; source `FeSO4(NH4)2SO4.6H2O`; raw source label `FeSO4(NH4)2SO4.6H2O`.\n- `CM_NAME:a0904f210b0689887db38c10d22989b237ba0a2a60d27f2801a85077d9ee6b6c`; source `(NH4)2SO4FeSO4 × 6H2O`; raw source label `(NH4)2SO4FeSO4 × 6H2O`.\n- `CM_NAME:ae541eb6dc54dff13a0406bbea554e9ed353683fe05493deb6192a5da62596f7`; source `(NH4)2Fe(SO4)2・6H2O`; raw source label `(NH4)2Fe(SO4)2・6H2O`.\n- `KG_CASE:43cc527abd97db8f30e73215d6cf922734ae7eec0fa7b9303c3bb4227558a0ea`; source `mediadive.ingredient:113`; raw source label `Na-pyruvate`.\n- `KG_CASE:4b7e86a2a10425a7d3777449e0375b761cb3821b26155e1e41bf69bf571e5e76`; source `mediadive.ingredient:106`; raw source label `Fe(NH4)2(SO4)2`.\n- `KG_CASE:a5de5680f410f37548a4708f6c56d5137e9140044007527774d011ae38029d60`; source `mediadive.ingredient:762`; raw source label `Na pyruvate`.\n- `KG_CASE:fa582b7326d5d9051fe2a53c1ed88df58acce880cd09ed3c2661153cf247fc15`; source `mediadive.ingredient:277`; raw source label `VOSO4 x 5 H2O`.\n\n- `c-chebi-76181`: [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:76181](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:76181); accessed `2026-11-08T05:07:38.350964+00:00`; `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/c/captures/chebi-76181.json` (SHA256 `7c66c3f2971ef73a26f7ac0530c5cb9e7fd9c279d28e0fb955d0e89b73260a45`).\n- `c-chebi-50144`: [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:50144](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:50144); accessed `2026-11-08T05:07:40.864927+00:00`; `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/c/captures/chebi-50144.json` (SHA256 `0d96d95af7783f3b4842a2c748e6e09e3e638436988b096aa19f377587f5d82c`).\n- `c-chebi-132758`: [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:132758](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:132758); accessed `2026-11-08T05:07:38.489048+00:00`; `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/c/captures/chebi-132758.json` (SHA256 `fb200a93b215d6811e2bd540688a2d217377cd502c9d84d7aaaf14a78f3b5b01`).\n- `c-chebi-87020`: [https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:87020](https://www.ebi.ac.uk/ols4/api/ontologies/chebi/terms?obo_id=CHEBI:87020); accessed `2026-11-08T05:07:37.863257+00:00`; `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/c/captures/chebi-87020.json` (SHA256 `fbf850a3ccae6ed0e62d3e78d0da4bd252a51af85a59c3d70294801eef4adaeb`).\n- `a-primary-atcc-2883`: [https://www.atcc.org/~/media/E4D6EB3B1C80408996E0DD53A0D258A1.ashx](https://www.atcc.org/~/media/E4D6EB3B1C80408996E0DD53A0D258A1.ashx); accessed `2026-11-08T05:25:43.510566+00:00`; `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/a/captures/atcc-2883-primary.pdf` (SHA256 `78179650fdbf7dcb07f6d07d0263470c64b732bfb44580478a5f9e67209448d9`).\n\nIndependent reviewer `/root/final_reviewer` approved the exact composed Mohr payload and its seven scoped cases in `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/continuation-1201-v1/d/independent-review-mohr-v2.json` (SHA256 `9b22001a7400cf1c979dc26ba526ade6155245d79502e564b46ed35bf98cbdab`). This is not a whole-owner, merge or publication approval.\nIndependent reviewer `/root/research_a` approved the exact pyruvate and vanadyl payloads within the declared C-review scope in `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/continuation-1201-v1/a/review-c/independent-review.json` (SHA256 `37577be2e1881e5e32fb430f68ffd15a7dedc86994b135c9bd5764f3b3116a71`). This is not a whole-owner, merge or publication approval.\nIndependent reviewer `/root/research_b` approved the exact methanol payload within the declared A-review scope in `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/continuation-1201-v1/b/independent-review-a-binder-v1.json` (SHA256 `f4521c3947dc1a79cde4b5ac94bae8770470cd4c2b83faeab6171b1c931a4206`). This is not a whole-owner, merge or publication approval.\n\nThe Mohr receipt binds the final composed successor, including all six preserved earlier source aliases and the three new rejections. Approval of C's isolated fragment alone was not treated as approval of that composition. Bare-formula, generic-hydrate, role-like and other full-owner obligations remain held.\n\nVanadyl requires cross-shard reconciliation: the captured coordinator observation records worker10 `chem-proposal-113` at head `dbaf4629f3b93d3bd8a78028e243abfe90c7a922`, payload `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-10/chemicals/proposed/Voso4_X_5_H2o.yaml`, SHA256 `7b38dec9fd6f28a46639ef4dd0f14d7c2bcd4db6c5bfca1f33f9dfe76fcbeef4`, against the same baseline owner. It proposes a source formula-ordering alias from TOGO M2262. That is a distinct delta from worker02's two rejections. Preserve both proposal histories and require independent review of the exact combined bytes before integration; this observation does not attest worker10's scientific review, choose a winner or approve worker10's source cases. Observation: `reports/all_unmatched_20261107/worker-02/continuation-1201-v1/validation/cross-shard-overlaps-v1.json` (SHA256 `5ff9da544c2b1bfa043712df04eedc85fda2d4942adb0a7b749f9692d9a280b3`).\n\nExisting #1189 covers glyoxylate, vanadate, AQDS and carbonate, not these four owners. #1203 concerns magnesium-sulfate stock occurrences. #702 mentions Na-pyruvate for a historical CAS-to-ChEBI import defect, and #752 mentions methanol within hydrogen-gas aliases; neither covers these exact tokens. This is a bounded related bundle, not a closure of those issues or #718's release umbrella. Keep the recorded Mohr, sodium-pyruvate and vanadyl WITHHOLD reasons and all other source/owner/release obligations until separately assessed.\n\nBefore applying any accepted delta, compare the then-current owner bytes and reconcile concurrent proposals. Preserve every raw label, original source reference, existing REJECTED_LABEL, WITHHOLD, source-quantity and downstream hold. Use guarded curation with history and the required maintained-surface/SSSOM synchronization and native validation. This draft requests no merge, downstream rebuild, automatic owner release or closure of broader issues.\n\n<!-- mim-review-round: worker02-continuation1201-v1 -->\n<!-- mim-review-bundle: new-pure-owner-qualified-aliases -->\n<!-- mim-fingerprints: 0e9bcfb4f0eaf50beefb3c1acbacc9f2a174b6d99ba22ed2738f6ee5f7ecbf3c,88defd96a502824a9c55ced34e60ef406af757f1033f33b506bfcaadd31be184,fd47fc3cb6f1875603d90fd0e81a0c2e8375b99de057d45cb1c1ead7a331d7d3,70913314a90cf18234d8d93a51d79bfe3cb41ade002718376845f2c8091cfc50 -->\n","number":1220,"state":"open","title":"Preserve stock and supplied-form boundaries in Mohr, pyruvate, vanadyl and methanol aliases","url":"https://github.com/CultureBotAI/MediaIngredientMech/issues/1220"},{"body":"The completed independent preparation-comparison packets identify duplicate proposed preparations, source-continuity conflicts and unsupported claims of disjointness. This issue tracks only the bounded family decisions below. These are isolated proposals; no record merge, new namespace, scientific approval or export release is authorized by the review.\n\nAll three sealed packets were independently hash-checked: Worker01 878 files, Worker05 390, Worker10 526, with no hash mismatch or unlisted file in the ignored-inclusive inventories. Their assignments partition the 67 mechanical family leads (26/22/19); this means comparison coverage, not 67 resolved or approved identities. The exact 28 retained finding/obligation IDs are reduced to 26 rows in `.temp/all-unmatched-20261107/preflight/family-findings-triage-v1/findings-matrix-v2.json`. Original authors, skeptical reviews, proposal bytes, primary capture times/hashes, source cases and occurrences remain immutable.\n\nA source accession, filename, receiving dose, missing carrier, unknown pH or unspecified hydrate does not prove a distinct supplied preparation. Nor does it prove equality. Source-qualified partial proposals remain useful; overlapping candidates need a defined scope or the missing evidence before simultaneous installation. No unknown is filled by guessing. Source-batch water and final-volume instructions remain separate, and immediate-list completeness is independent of molecular grounding.\n\n| Findings / frozen entries | Sourced conclusion and bounded next action |\n|---|---|\n| W01-FPC-PA-001 + MIN-F03; 573/810, maintained ATCC_Wolfes_Vitamin_Mix | JCM197, NBRC837 and NBRC903 give the same ten nominal vitamins and amounts plus1L water. Prepare one combined nominal candidate preserving all source-specific processing. The maintained ATCC owner has authentic branded MD-VS history and a D-(+) calcium-pantothenate specification; JCM/NBRC only say calcium pantothenate. Preserve that distinction in what the evidence asserts: unspecified stereo proves neither sameness nor difference. Do not automatically reuse ATCC or install two source-number owners. Establish the applicability bridge or explicitly decide nominal-recipe versus supplied-product scope before co-installation. |\n| MIN-F01; 624/657 | DSM590/1144 Hutner tables and preparation match at nominal scope. Preserve CaCl2·2H2O3.335g versus3.34g rounding and both malformed molybdate strings as literal unresolved assertions; do not turn a typographical discrepancy into a different chemical. Prepare one source-union nominal recipe candidate. Both underlying Metals44 instructions are retained; the current automatically extracted portal is not a historical erratum. |\n| MIN-F02, W05-CR-F02; 381–384/624/657/705 | Wolfe JCM470/DSM792, modified Wolfe ATCC1190/1191 versus JCM221, and Hutner JCM900/979 comparisons have explicit unresolved hydrate/reagent or preparation details. Correct claims that missing qualifiers prove incompatibility. Do not infer JCM470's variable Mn hydrate as monohydrate, or transfer ATCC final-volume/form-specific instructions to JCM221. Preserve the positively different JCM149 MgSO4 quantity14.45g versus29.7g. |\n| W01-FPC-PA-003; 747 plus existing JCM403 B12 owner | NBRC1321 explicitly gives cyanocobalamin5mg with100ml water; JCM403 specifies generic B12 at matching nominal quantities. Preserve both levels of specificity. Missing JCM vitamer/preparation evidence is an unresolved relation, not a proved difference or an exact identity bridge. Coordinate the existing JCM403 promotion/pointer correction under1201/1227; do not create a competing owner by accession alone. |\n| W01-PREP-B-001; 619 | NBRC1507 names0.1M Tris/HCl pH7.5 stock but does not list free hydrochloric acid as a separate component. Remove that unsupported free-acid has-part claim. Preserve the literal named buffer, strength and pH with unknown complete composition; do not substitute dry Tris-HCl salt or invent solvent/neutralization. |\n| W01-PREP-B-002 + CHEM-COMP-003; 669 | JCM1479 positively specifies a5% L-cysteine-HCl-monohydrate stock atpH7. Unreported pH of other5% stocks does not establish a different substance. Correct the comparison wording, retain stock/solid separation and the unknown percentage basis/carrier/titrant. |\n| CHEM-COMP-002; 6/13 | NBRC1020 prints Na2WO4; JCM317 explicitly prints dihydrate, both at4mg with4mg selenite and1L water. Remove the claim that omission proves anhydrous NBRC1020 or disjointness. Preserve both literal tables and ask only for the missing supplied form if full chemical equivalence is needed. |\n| CHEM-COMP-004; 943/944/946/106 | Literal35%,32%,25% HCl and qualitative concentrated labels have unknown comparable bases; M2305/M2746 even call their25% input concentrated. Correct categorical disjointness without converting percentages or inventing a carrier. Retain source qualification; an explicit common partial-material scope or comparable formulation evidence is needed before consolidation. |\n| BIO-COMP-005; 328/333 with283/287/288/290 | Historical MJ and JCM1216 0.1x artificial-seawater formulations remain partly unspecified. Missing recipe/version is not evidence of a different formulation. Preserve the source-qualified preparations, positive known differences and exact missing historical MJ/1x-base specification; no guessed formula or wholesale seawater merge. |\n| BIO-COMP-001; 201/476 | CM0643 prepared broth and dry powder are different supplied forms. The source handles for entry201 use1000ml/10ml broth; entry476 weighs33g powder. Correct entry201's dry-powder representation and account for its authentic existing broth provenance. Retain powder separate from prepared broth, water and receiving supplements; the same catalogue does not erase the supplied-form boundary. MICRO:0002186 describes liquid, so any use requires whole-broth§3 scope review and must not identify powder. |\n| BIO-F02; 971 + Swine_Serum | The new DSM1076b heat-inactivated swine-serum proposal uses MediaDive960, already the creation source of Swine_Serum/UNMAPPED_0536. Reconcile or promote through that authentic preimage/history. Do not add a second same-source owner or label the separate generic Porcine_Serum/MD967 untreated. Heat schedule remains unknown. |\n| BIO-F03; 970 + Bovine_Calf_Serum | JCM1303 heat-inactivated calf serum uses MediaDive2061, already the import source of Bovine_Calf_Serum. Audit its broader/Gibco occurrences and partition their applicability before narrowing or adding an owner. Missing historical heat metadata is not an untreated claim. No wholesale repurposing or maintained-owner merge. |\n| BIO-F04; 893/908/914/916/922 | Withdraw unsupported serum exclusions: bovine does not exclude fetal; gamma irradiation does not exclude heat treatment; unspecified heat schedule need not differ from a specified one. Retain positive age/species/catalogue/process facts and actual30/45/60minute or active/inactivated differences. No forced product equivalence. |\n| BIO-F05; 904/906 | JCM946 supports56C30min heating and filtration before addition, but not their relative order. Clarify only that ordering claim. DSM1021 explicitly requires sterile fetal/newborn alternatives; preserve sterility for the selected newborn scope without inventing heat or filter treatment. |\n| BIO-F06; 300/921 | Oxoid CM0331 and TOGO M2224 disclose the same nominal dry base: special peptone23g, starch1g, NaCl5g, agar10g, pH7.3±0.2. Prepare one combined formulation candidate while retaining which source actually states the catalogue. Before installation, account for existing Columbia_Blood_Agar_Base's mixed Oxoid/Difco provenance; do not repurpose the entire owner. Preserve the distinct Difco/BBL/EH formulations. Blood and reconstitution water are not dry-base parts. |\n| BIO-F07; 980 | Replace a search-wrapper-as-primary assertion with the recovered2009 BD manufacturer manual capture, p158. Keep original wrapper, older manual edition and failed URLs as historical evidence. This verifies the nominal Difco formulation, not a historical lot or arbitrary vendor equivalence. |\n| BIO-F08; 919 | Current ATCC0988 is explicitly reformulated asMD2611 and specifies ATCC30-2020 plus55C treatment; frozen TOGO M2578 preserves older fetal/newborn alternatives and unknown schedule. Keep both versions and their exact applicability. Same URL is not same document; this is a version obligation, not a finding that the frozen transcription is false. |\n| CHEM-COMP-006; 35/36 | Reassess new claim-specific resolver dispositions. The fully specified0.01M FeSO4·7H2O in0.02N HCl name is not shown to be a non-name merely because a global alias was undesirable. Bicarbonate footnote pointers have different ambiguity. Preserve all existing rejected entries; do not blanket-reactivate or blanket-reject authentic labels. Under§3, any new rejection needs claim-specific evidence; owned-name suppression applies only when its ownership condition holds. Historical1173 lineage is not a new scientific decision. |\n\nAdditional reconciliation groups with positive evidence can proceed to isolated candidate preparation, with exact-byte independent review before application:\n\n- DAIGO395-01681 entries188/474: one named dry product, eight manufacturer components. Preserve the manufacturer/JCM peptone wording and exact hydrate, the3.15g listed sum versus3.2g preparation instruction, and both histories. Do not invent another constituent, agar, water, generic DSM1537 applicability or wholesale KG1402 routing. The local identifier is already shared; choose one readable destination by the product scope, not author order.\n- Mixed phosphate entries873/940: one nominal preparation from equal volumes of1M KH2PO4 and1M Na2HPO4. Preserve50+50ml versus10+10ml batches and PBBM-onlypH7.2. The immediate input list can be complete without claiming its input stocks' exact hydrate, solvent or neutralization chemistry.\n- HEPES-KOH1M entries449/450 (W05-CR-F01): both sources positively name the same nominal strength/neutralizer; receiving-mediumpH7.14/9.0 is not stockpH. Recommend an explicit common bounded nominal scope if that is the intended owner model; otherwise retain candidate holds for actual stockpH/carrier/neutralization evidence. Do not install two proved-distinct preparations based solely on source numbers.\n- 95% ethanol entries460–463 (W05-CR-F03): preserve proven within-protocol reuse and every occurrence. A shared bounded partial-material scope is an option, but neither four distinct complete formulations nor equality follows without percentage basis/carrier/denaturant/product evidence. Do not infer95%v/v aqueous NCIT identity. Missing composition is not permission to discard the supported partial material.\n\nExisting trackers are reused, not duplicated:1206 JCM852;1210 sodium-thiosulfate tetrahydrate;1202 Polypeptone;1212 Phytone/SoyPeptone;1217 W06 source/solvent provenance;1221 EBIOS;1204 rumen. For rumen the current sourced decision explicitly leaves the three dependent parents' literal rumen-fluid components UNMAPPED; the older comparison suggestion to redirect them to clarified fluid is superseded, not fresh evidence. The Tris-HCl parent-grade defect is filed separately because its exact record correction/native repro is distinct from these formulation decisions.\n\nPrimary source anchors: [JCM197](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=197), [NBRC903](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=903), [ATCC2672](https://www.atcc.org/-/media/product-assets/documents/microbial-media-formulations/2/6/7/2/atcc-medium-2672.pdf?rev=7f27672230474579b9151e4c2ec9f20a), [DSM590](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium590.pdf), [DSM1144](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1144.pdf), [JCM470](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=470), [NBRC1507](https://www.nite.go.jp/nbrc/catalogue/NBRCMediumDetailServlet?NO=1507), [DSM1076b](https://www.dsmz.de/microorganisms/medium/pdf/DSMZ_Medium1076b.pdf), [JCM1303](https://www.jcm.riken.jp/cgi-bin/jcm/jcm_grmd?GRMD=1303), [Oxoid CM0331 specification](https://documents.thermofisher.com/TFS-Assets/MBD/Specification-Sheets/PS-CM0331-V6.pdf), [TOGO M2224](https://togomedium.org/sparqlist/api/gmdb_medium_by_gmid?gm_id=M2224), [BD2009 manual](https://fsl.nmsu.edu/documents/difcobblmanual_2nded_lowres.pdf), [DAIGO manufacturer](https://labchem-wako.fujifilm.com/jp/product/detail/W01N0139-0168.html). Every capture's exact original URL/time/hash and case binding is retained in the triage indexes and source packets; links alone are not treated as immutable evidence.\n\nDo not apply the original frozen W06 payloads just because their historical paths still exist. Six selected W06 payloads and its new EBIOS proposal have advanced and need exact successor comparisons. W07's observed successor was metadata-only in the source comparison, but its actual selected bytes still require final intake readback. All source, role and release holds remain content-bound.\n\nExact frozen source origins retained for these findings (later successors require explicit bridges):\n\n| Entry | Original proposal | Source head | Exact payload SHA256 |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 6 | `w01::NSV4-PROP-NBRC_1020_Se_W_Solution` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `235072e64c69a7dc51f9386f0664d69ffab234a5a0cca427cf4b4b18b37de0e7` |\n| 13 | `w01::NSV4-PROP-JCM_317_Se_W_Solution` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `1603001c438fc6e321f1f105cff5ebd5a9f2be169e5657493de1d8b49a4ace62` |\n| 35 | `w01::CS-PROP-JCM1430_FERROUS_SULFATE_HCL_STOCK` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `6e0ae3d8ec0984d7e29034b2fd41d3589f26fb7f236bdcc7a829d632837e0c59` |\n| 36 | `w01::CS-PROP-NBRC1321_CO2_BICARBONATE_STOCK` | `26445f23b5a905ac26d864acfbd658570c88769c` | `61c0a226a8a99d96b43657f6e00075e901ce051a698b01bd99f6ab6f1d88717c` |\n| 106 | `w02::a2-proposal-togo-m2746-m2305-hydrochloric-acid-25percent` | `0597d00417be4d7cdfb5a31970043eec9bbc88fe` | `7